        "original_id": "fe1efbaa-9853-51b2-a794-a1dcef9afc85",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Dressing Point massacre\n- People: Karankawa people, White colonists\n- Places: Mexican Texas, Matagorda, Tejas, Coahuila, Coahuila y Tejas\n- Concepts: 1824 Constitution of Mexico, federal structure\n\nFacts:\n- In 1824, the Constitution of Mexico established a federal structure.\n- In 1824, the province of Tejas and the province of Coahuila were joined to form the state of Coahuila y Tejas.\n- In 1826, the Dressing Point massacre occurred in Mexican Texas near present-day Matagorda.\n- In 1826, a party of White colonists murdered 40–50 Karankawa people in the Dressing Point massacre.",
